From d8f8247a7acd0f76687bb2c9524522a6f3a2a18f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:45:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] web: an event in a text field says where the caret is,
 and a program can move it

ElementEvent gains selStart and selEnd: the selectionStart and selectionEnd
of the <input> or <textarea> the event happened in, read when it happened,
-1 elsewhere. Element.select(start, end) sets them, and like a rendered
value it does not land over typing the program has not seen yet.

An editor needs both: Tab, auto-indent and a line:column readout need the
caret, and going to a line needs to put it there. Asked for by the wac IDE.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J7c8hTEmTN5s7KvmrRMqXX
